    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d16">

                <pb facs="0039" n="773" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg773"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr. Young.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-15"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 172.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 161, of February
                    21, 1895, in relation to the cases of W. H. Argall, Henry Thomas, and Robert
                    Pardee, American citizens in prison at Guatemala City.</p>
                <pb facs="0040" n="774" xml:id="pg774"/>
                <p>Shortly after the receipt of your dispatch Mr. Gresham orally called the matter
                    to the attention of the Guatemalan minister, and referred particularly to the
                    fact that Mr. Argall, while so imprisoned, was scourged with a rawhide whip. Mr.
                    Lazo Arriaga then promised to communicate with his Government and to inform us
                    of the result.</p>
                <p>No reply having been received from that gentleman, I addressed him a note upon
                    the subject on the 11th instant,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d16-f1"/> a copy of which
                    I inclose for your information.</p>
                <p>The minister replied on the 12th instant, stating that he had promptly requested
                    his Government to furnish him with the necessary information, and that he had
                    been advised that it intended doing so at an early date.</p>
                <p>You will ascertain and report such additional facts in relation to the case of
                    these American citizens as you may be able to obtain.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
